    "note": "Morschhauser, Grott & Breuer 2011's thermal-evolution model prints a present-day stagnant-lid thickness of 330 km for Mars (2011Icar..212..541M:1457–1459, cache text layer; the paper defines `Dl` as the lid base at :274, not an elastic or seismic thickness — so it is the quantity eq. (3) takes). It is a model output, not an observation, which is why the grade is analog. Breuer & Spohn 2003's 350–500 km band brackets it from above; the ~250 km elastic thickness is a different quantity and neither confirms nor refutes it. The refutation site is an observational lid-base thickness, an InSight-class result, not another model.\n"
